  "id": "COMPOUND:22485 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Javanicoside F appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to RWLeu4, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first evidence points to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by Javanicoside F and in turn targets RWLeu4. The second path links Javanicoside F to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which also targets RWLeu4. The third path identifies Javanicoside F as a target of a dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase, which in turn targets RWLeu4. These findings collectively suggest that Javanicoside F may act through multiple pathways to influence RWLeu4, potentially through protein degradation or kinase inhibition. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Javanicoside F and RWLeu4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on RWLeu4 indicates a possible role in cellular regulation, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism.",
